    "graph_me_drives": {
      "request": "GET https://dav.example.com/graph/v1.0/me/drives",
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json; charset=utf-8"
        },
        "body": {
          "value": [
            {
              "id": "personal$root",
              "driveType": "personal",
              "name": "Personal",
              "eTag": "\"root-etag\"",
              "root": {
                "id": "personal$root",
                "eTag": "\"root-etag\"",
                "webDavUrl": "https://dav.example.com/dav/spaces/personal$root"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invariants": [
        "Both top-level eTag and root.eTag MUST be populated and change together: Desktop Space::setDrive checks root.eTag (space.cpp:65-72), whereas ETagWatcher::slotSpaceChanged reads top-level OAIDrive::getETag via space->eTag() (space.cpp:140, etagwatcher.cpp:39, OAIDrive.cpp:201,436).",
        "drive.id must equal drive.root.id: SpacesManager keys spaces by drive.id while Space::id returns root.id.",
        "root.webDavUrl MUST omit any trailing slash and use literal '$' (not '%24'): Android RemoteFile.getRemotePathFromUrl URL-decodes href before splitting by spaceWebDavUrl (RemoteFile.kt:190-198).",
        "quota (nullable on Android; when present quota.total is non-null Long), owner, special, webUrl, description, and virtual/shares are safe to omit."
      ]
    }
